 "body": "<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\n## Summary\n\nA finished webhook review is posted as one pull-request review with event COMMENT. The payload builder has no event argument. `APPROVE` and `REQUEST_CHANGES` are refused before any request. The body says the review is advisory and not a substitute for the full Claude Code protocol review, then lists lenses run and not run, the file-coverage note, limit stops, and cost. D46 records the choice, the options that were not taken, the cost, and the relation to D24, D25, D37, D53, D45 and D48. It does not claim the 1 GB volume; that volume exists only when D53's app is deployed.\n\nA failed review posts nothing. The marker counts only when `commit_id` is this SHA and the author is this App's bot (`ATLAS_GITHUB_APP_SLUG` plus `[bot]`). Immediately before the create, the worker re-checks under the queue lock. A review GitHub has already accepted cannot be recalled. Each attempt's 45-second deadline includes the token mint, and `limit_timeout` is the mint socket timeout. A 403 is a rate limit only when `Retry-After` is present, or the remaining budget is 0, or the body names a secondary limit. A secondary limit waits at least 60 seconds. A 401, any other 403, and a 422 are not retried. A 422 is logged as `post rejected`, not as an auth refusal. `stop()` does not send a post that was only deferred, including one whose draft is already on disk, and a stop that lands after the post is claimed is not sent. `limit_timeout` is per thread and is cleared after the mint. Each worker keeps its own 45-second attempt deadline. The posted comment does not include the draft's review narrative. A token mint that hits a secondary rate limit is retried. A mint 401 is not. The review list asks for 100 reviews per page. The posting token refuses an allowlist that spans two GitHub accounts. D46 records that this service defaults to `openrouter`. The comment scrubber and the service log both cover the webhook secret, the App key, the Sprites token, the OpenRouter key, and minted tokens.\n\nHead: `72c56eb24d16025719c4d58ba921eadef94bb8a8`\n\nCI on that commit: https://github.com/brandondees/code-quality-atlas/actions/runs/43510622915 (success). `atlas_reviewer` coverage **96.82%** (2137 passed, floor 94%). The tooling suite in the same run was 95.20% (873 passed, 14 skipped).\n\n#639 is merged. This targets main.\n\n## Risk\n\nThe token can create a COMMENT on `brandondees/code-quality-atlas`. It cannot send APPROVE or REQUEST_CHANGES. A bug can leave an advisory comment on a public pull request. The App private key stays in the parent process. A create that GitHub has already accepted cannot be taken back.\n\n## Rollback\n\nDo not deploy this branch by itself. If a later deploy posts comments that should stop, disable the repository webhook and stop `atlas-reviewer-service`. The one-off app is unchanged. These tests use fakes. Nothing was posted to GitHub from this change.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `APPROVE` and `REQUEST_CHANGES` raise `RefusedReviewEvent` and send no HTTP request\n- a successful post is one COMMENT whose body has the banner and the five lists\n- a planted Sprites token, OpenRouter key, and minted installation token do not appear in the posted body\n- the service log scrubs those same secrets (`test_the_service_log_scrubs_the_sprites_and_openrouter_secrets`)\n- a secret and `<!--` markup planted in a report field do not appear raw in the posted body\n- a `Link` next that leaves the API raises `BoundaryError` and is not followed\n- a 403 with `x-ratelimit-reset` and remaining greater than 0 raises `PostAuthError`; remaining 0 waits\n- a `Retry-After` above 15 minutes is capped at 900 seconds, and a bare 403 is not retried\n- a secondary rate limit with no headers waits 60 seconds\n- a 422 raises `PostRejected`, the worker settles `FAILED`, and a retry does not post again (`test_a_rejected_post_fails_without_a_retry`)\n- another App's `[bot]` login does not suppress the post\n- the head is re-checked after the list and before the create\n- a token mint that consumes the 45-second deadline sends no request\n- `limit_timeout` is the timeout passed to the mint socket (`test_limit_timeout_is_the_mint_socket_timeout`)\n- `stop()` during an in-flight create does not send a deferred post that already has a draft (`test_stop_does_not_send_a_deferred_post`)\n- a stop that lands after the post is claimed does not send (`test_stop_after_the_post_is_claimed_does_not_send`)\n- `limit_timeout` on another thread does not change this thread's mint, and the value does not stick (`test_limit_timeout_stays_on_the_calling_thread`)\n- one worker finishing does not clear another's attempt deadline (`test_one_workers_deadline_does_not_clear_anothers`)\n- a hostile `## Review narrative` is not posted, and the event stays COMMENT (`test_a_hostile_narrative_is_not_posted`)\n- `claim_post` refuses a stopped worker (`test_claim_post_refuses_a_stopped_worker`)\n- the loop does not retry a post after stop (`test_the_loop_does_not_retry_a_post_after_stop`)\n- a stopped worker does not claim a deferred post (`test_retry_post_does_not_claim_after_stop`)\n- backoff jitter is pinned by `test_the_post_backoff_includes_jitter`, which merged in #639\n- a corrupt `posted.json` makes `main` exit 2\n- a second post, and a post after the local record is dropped, do not create another review\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a href=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-cc3a34d1-fe9e-5172-91b2-646c0bec1b42?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img alt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-cc3a34d1-fe9e-5172-91b2-646c0bec1b42&cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_cursor\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-light.png\"><img alt=\"Open in Cursor\" width=\"131\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;</div>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added webhook-triggered pull request reviews that post advisory comments on the reviewed commit.\n  * Prevented duplicate comments when a matching review already exists.\n  * Added safeguards for review posting, including comment-only submissions and bounded retries for temporary failures.\n  * Kept operator-triggered reviews as drafts without posting them to GitHub.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Clarified service setup, credentials, posting permissions, and review behavior.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
